New in 1.93.1
Updates registration system.
disabled the turning with q and e when you're in a vehicle.
If you draw a weapon that makes you walk slower, your jumping speed gets cut back too.
fixed the camra, thanks silak.
Removes voicechat from the game.
New in 1.93.0
**Game is now paid! Blame all the cheaters for it.
Added a brand new registration system to the game!
The inventory menu will process all events now, not just network. Meaning you can't hang in the air and stuff.
New in 1.92.2
Communication of coordinates from client to server and back is now fully floating point, meaning sounds and such should play from the correct position when rotation is involved. Output to the user, such as tracking and pressing c, however, is rounded for user's convenience.
Updates game engine to 0.8.0.0.
Fixes speech interrupt.
Completely recoded the inventory menu, so no more runtime errors! As a drawback, shift enter to use an item from within the menu no longer works.
You can now hear when people scroll through their inventory.
Fixes runtime error in voice selection menu using DFSpeech.
Good luck turning off your internet to open multiple instances of the game!
Changes window title.
Improves updater code, it is now a lot faster!
New in 1.92.1:
Added the ability to toggle speech interrupt. Go do this in options if you need to.
Updates GameEngine to 0.7.
Zones now interrupt.
Changed some options around to make the menu more clean, at least to me, sorry OCD about toggles and other menus being in a certain order.
Beta members, you no longer need to remember your info or match everything you do on the current and beta server because we save the client's data in another file if you're  running a beta build of the game!
Slight changes to the jumping system. now you can jump on  platforms above you.
Fixes a bug with server-side menus.
Fixes inventory position not syncing with the server.
Fixes inventory descriptions.
Fixes small undetected loophole in the banning system.
Removes underscores from the inventory menu.
Fixed menu first letter navigation.
More checks to GameEngine.dll actually being in the tk directory.
Fixes MOTD not being grabbed on startup.
New in 1.92.0: 
Corrects the updater so you don't get a runtime error if the version is out of date or you are not connected to the internet.
Changes version number and changes updater to support this change.
Completely redesigns the store system! Shelters now have a store you can brows and shop for items. Note: when using the shelter store, items are cheaper!
Adds shipments to the game!
There are multiple stores if you enter the store map. Have fun!
Speeds up the camera.
added shift+f5 to copy the player's name to the clipboard
You can now toggle buffer interrupt when speaking. Press backslash to toggle the currently focused buffer between interrupt and non-interrupt.
Updates map engine to the Masonasons engine!
Because of the Map engine upgrades, access to the map stats for admins and developers is no longer supported.
Very slight updates to readme.txt.
Fixes select menu music bug, and the failure to exit if menu music was set to a sound that couldn't be loaded.
Fixes escape in options menu breaking in unexpected ways.
New in 1.91
Adds the ability to drop items. Press shift backspace to drop the item.
Fixes a bug where the zone tracker would report information if you weren't tracking anything.
Menu dynamic music updates.
Adds MS conversion in the pinging information if the ping is grader than 1000 ms which is equal to a complete second.
New in 1.9
*** This update is mainly focused on things like player inventories and making the game a lot more fun for everyone.
Removed bikes for now.
Reintroduced doors, (please report if something is wrong) they could be unstable.
Fixed bug that was causing to play the vehicle engine loop in the main menu after client disconnects
Finally fixed the camera. the camera now works properly.
The store is now a safe zone. When you die you will spawn in the store.
After work to server, items will no longer save after character death. This update will not be released for 2 days after the update to give everyone an equal chance to store their items in shelters or lockers.
Added small lockers to put your items in! These lockers can be asigned by going to 5, 5, 0 at the store. Please note: you must have 10 metal and 250 coins to do this.
Removed /flag.
Makes the game load all sounds(excluding ambiences and music) into memory. Note: this may affect loading times, but CPU will greatly be improved.
Weapon system slightly redone.
Disables running.
No more going into input boxes to stay in the air while falling!
Fixes bugs with jumping and moving down.
New in 1.81
Added 3 new ambiences and a surface to the builder.
Fixed runtime error in inventory menu.
Changed air key to alt+r.
Adds a new system to unstun yourself if you are stunned. Press the X key over and over until you hear a little sound. Move away quickly or you will be zapped again!
Adds/redesigns weapon system, allowing us to support reloading of weapons.
New in 1.80
*** this update was rushed because I won't be around for a month, needed to fix the main problems cheaters were using. If there are bugs, updates will folllow. The main bulk of the update will be handled through the server. This update just handles what it needs to.
Added TK dollars. These dollars are available in minigames or the TK store. Each dollar is about 5000 coins.
Added antibiotic canisters.
You can now get drunk in TK!
CPU fixes.
Weapons support walking speed now.
After work to server, a new minigame (double or nothing) (played with coins you have) will be available.
After work to server, capture the flag will be available.
There are now multiple tracks in the main menu!
Added minigames!
Added a bunch of new kill messages thanks to FrightnIght!
You can no longer create multiple accounts!
No more opening multiple instances of the game, sorry cheaters.
Added events to the killer! If admins want they can start events now. I.E: tankfight events, item collecting events, etc.
Adds vending machines!
Adds a food system.
You should no longer hit walls repeatedly.
Camera can move into the negatives now, since people love to build there.
Finally fully fixes not being able to connect without restarting client!
Makes falling system to be a bit more realistic. If you fall, you will need to stand back up. Press S to do this.
Turned mouse detection off for now.
Fixes remote guns connection bug.
New in 1.702
Adds the ability to give items to people. Press shift space in the inventory menu.
Added air canisters, drop some on the ground, and you and people nearby will get some air.
Added gas masks, put one on if you are going under water! If you dont' have one on you will drown. Please make sure you have air on you, press R to check!
You may now press escape while in the death phase to get the exit menu, for those who want to ragequit.
Adds the ability to fire with the mouse.
You should still receive network events while a map is in loading phase, this will prevent lag bursts while loading main etc.
Adds a new map feature called ambiences, kind of like sources, where you can cover an area with a sound loop. The difference here is ambiences will just go silent when you are not in them, while sources kind of pan away. Syntax is amb:minx:maxx:miny:maxy:minz:maxz:sound. Also available in builder menu!
Edits map code to allow you to climb below z 0 if there is a platform down there, can be used for something like the bottom of the river. For this reason, also extends falling code to detect if you are falling into air in the negatives, and if that's the case, will jump you back up to z 1 and have you land safely.
Adds more map sounds.
Adds the ability to turn with the mouse. You can turn this on in settings.
Makes inventory menu just focus the item if shift isn't down.
Fixes a bug with the moving sound handler that would not stop the moving sound when it was out of range sometimes.
New in 1.701
Fixes bugs with team and private messages.
Made it vary hard to screw with the speedhack detection code!
After work to server, the moving sound handler will no longer play sounds if they are out of earshot. This should significantly decrease the lag, as the update packets will no longer be sent to you if it is not necesary.
Removes pitch decrease for sound sources.
New in 1.70
Adds a shelter alarm if the shelter door is broken.
Added the ability to detect if the game is running from dropbox, and if it is, will not export logs.
Adds language channels!
Adds wirebombs, bombs with electric wires sticking out! If a player gets near a wirebomb, they will be stunned for a few seconds and they might die.
Adds a few new ambiences to the map builder.
Adds a store to TK! Unlike the old store, this store will move every 15 minutes.
Adds the FRNTAssaultRifle!
Adds an application to the shelter computer called SH pay, enabling you to send coins to other shelters!
Adds power to shelters! Fuel tanks should work on them. You can always cut the power at 12,12,0. Please do note that when the power is off, you will not have alarms and the computer will not be accessible to you.
Adds carrier missiles! These missiles can load items and take them to the entered coordinates provided.
Default health is 10000 now.
If your tank gets shot down, you no longer die instantly, however you might die still. You will lose anywhere from 20000 to 70000 health.
Fixes BGT runtime error if control is pressed while logging in.
Fixes a bug where moving sounds would not shut off after switching maps.
Tracker reports if player is below or above you.
Fixes camera wouldn't play when moving up or down.
New in 1.62
Fixes the Camera! You can move the camera in whatever direction your facing now.
New in 1.612
This update was prompted by player action. Edits ban system.
New in 1.611
Makes new sounds file work with new versions.
Fixes runtimes with builder.
New in 1.61
Readme has been vastly updated with new information!
Updater is now a menu for wine users, etc.
Edits weapon system to get its data from the server, so we can update weapon times and add new weapons without pushing a client update.
Edits favorite item system to support up to 6 items! Also eliminates the duplicate favorite item spamming.
The select soundcard feature should actually work now.
Menus no longer require the registry to store music volume, which should make this game run on school and other non-admin systems fine. IT stores it in prefs instead.
Vastly improves building prompts
Now, in order to be tracked from the menu, map zones must explicitly specify this via an extra parameter, though it really doesn't matter the contents. The builder prompts have support for this and will append :trackme if you want it to be found.
Sources no longer require you to explicitly specify an ID in the map string. The builder also reflects this change.
New in 1.60
+adds dynamic areas on the map like the store where you can not use certain items.
+ Ads impact bombs! These bombs will explode on impact. Meaning, timebombs, motion bombs, etc will make it blow up!
+ Added ultrabomb silencers. These are very simple and self-explanitory. When you have one in your inventory, use them on the ultrabomb's tile and the generator sound will die instantly.
* Teams have been slightly recoded. Teams will now save across server reboots and fixes lots of team bugs when logging in and out.
+ Finally added an ammo system!
+machinegun is back! Firing in bursts of 3, this weapon is mainly designed to take out a shield.
+adds right control detection. This is basically right control to fire since that's all control is used for at the moment. You can find it in the options menu.
*changed the uploaded sounds toggle to only work with sounds uploaded through the upload sound facility, voicechats will go through regardless.
-removed: background music.
* By request, the camera plays steps in higher pitches again.
New in 1.5321 patch
Fixed a nasty bug with the speedhack checker that would kick you off in menus.
New in 1.532
*** reenabled speedhack protection.
+adds the ability to know the name of a sound source in the builder menu by pressing tab.
*Now tracking can be accomplished by t or f5.
New in 1.531
+ Adds the ability to reset your password via e-mail varification. For this to work, we have added a command for setting up an email if you already have an account. Just type /setemail followed by your email. The server sends back a confirmation message to let you know everything went well.
* Recoded updater with new version, completely changing the update process. TK will no longer download an entire 100 mb file if it doesn't need to. Because of this, you don't need to extract a zip file, and the game should update all on its own!
New in 1.53
* Changed server.
+ Adds: Pressing F8 will now mute your tts.
+Adds: Over 50 new ambiences for builders.
+ Adds: Runs counter reports how many more times the game has been played since you last played the game.
New in 1.52
+Added: Ultrabombs. Ultrabombs are back, however not as deadly as they once were. They have a massive range of 75 tiles however. Place an ultrabomb, wait until its done. Open your inventory and add coins to them! Once they reach 50 coins, run away before it blasts you in the face. I really hope you're quick...
+Added: Sound updating. We can now update the sounds of the game with out the client doing a lot of work or even requiring an entire client update!
